From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:48:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Mark a :has() anchor's ancestors dirty after a tree-mutation
 invalidation

blitz 0.3.0-beta.3's TElement::set_dirty_descendants marks only the node
itself, because stylo calls it on nodes it is already traversing. The
tree-mutation pass runs the relative-selector invalidator outside any
traversal, and stylo propagates dirty_descendants only from what it
restyled up to the :has() anchor. On a removal that runs before the
unlink, so remove_node's own mark_ancestors_dirty then stopped at the
anchor's set bit, and the root-to-anchor path stayed clean. The
traversal never reached the anchor's subject, which kept its matched
style (WPT has-in-parent-position and has-in-ancestor-position).

Mark the anchor's ancestors from the invalidated callback, which is what
the callback is for. The snapshot pass needs no change: its mutation
already marked the spine above every anchor it can find.
---
 src/stylo.rs | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/stylo.rs b/src/stylo.rs
index 3749027..d2f7f6f 100644
--- a/src/stylo.rs
+++ b/src/stylo.rs
@@ -421,7 +421,20 @@ impl crate::document::BaseDocument {
             element,
             quirks_mode: self.stylist.quirks_mode(),
             snapshot_table: Some(&self.snapshots),
-            invalidated: |_, _| {},
+            // The invalidator propagates `dirty_descendants` from what it
+            // restyles up to the anchor only. `set_dirty_descendants` does not
+            // mark ancestors, so the anchor's own ancestors stay clean
+            // unless this marks them. A removal runs this before unlinking, and
+            // its own `mark_ancestors_dirty` from the parent then stops at the
+            // already-set anchor, so the traversal never reached the subject.
+            invalidated: |anchor, result| {
+                if result.has_invalidated_self()
+                    || result.has_invalidated_descendants()
+                    || result.has_invalidated_siblings()
+                {
+                    anchor.mark_ancestors_dirty();
+                }
+            },
             sibling_traversal_map: SiblingTraversalMap::default(),
             _marker: PhantomData,
         }
